1
00:00:00,099 --> 00:00:01,480
Run your thumb around the edge of a quarter

2
00:00:01,519 --> 00:00:03,159
and you'll feel ridges, which is a strange

3
00:00:03,199 --> 00:00:04,900
thing to put on a coin containing nothing worth

4
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:05,600
stealing.

5
00:00:05,679 --> 00:00:07,199
Back when coins were actually silver,

6
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,880
people shaved slivers off the rims,

7
00:00:09,159 --> 00:00:11,079
spent the coin anyway, and kept the shavings.

8
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,039
A shaved coin looked almost normal.

9
00:00:13,380 --> 00:00:14,839
So mints cut grooves into the edge,

10
00:00:15,019 --> 00:00:17,199
and a shaved coin stopped looking normal immediately,

11
00:00:17,399 --> 00:00:18,519
because the pattern just ended.

12
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:20,760
Isaac Newton used it against clippers as warden

13
00:00:20,779 --> 00:00:21,459
of the Royal Mint.

14
00:00:21,719 --> 00:00:22,799
The silver is long gone.

15
00:00:22,939 --> 00:00:23,679
The ridges stayed.
